    "reasoning": "All 16 current selections agree with independently verified mathematics and their own captured worked solutions. No submitted grades were supplied; every MA attribution below uses worked-solution evidence. For q-126838, r(\\pi)=⟨-1,0⟩ and r′(\\pi)=⟨0,1⟩ determine the tangent line. For q-126898, the perpendicularity condition is 2t=0, giving (0,4). For q-164838, r·r′=2t+2=0 gives t=-1 and (1,\\sqrt{2}). For q-165040, parallelism requires 8-4t=0, hence t=2; r′(2)=⟨2,4,0⟩ and r(2)=⟨0,4,8⟩. Its source incorrectly mentions ⟨0,1,3⟩ in one sentence, but the actual equations and final answer use the requested vector ⟨1,2,0⟩. For q-165042, the exponential components force proportionality factor 1/2, and the remaining equation gives t²=0, hence (1,1/2). For q-131485, back substitution gives x=-7z-3 and y=2z+2. For q-37649, R₂←R₂+2R₁ and R₃←R₃-3R₁ give the selected echelon matrix. For q-73913, x=-9+2y-7z; for q-131499, x=-2+4y-3z, yielding the selected vector parametrizations. For q-131519, the last row requires 0=-8, so there is no solution. For q-73959, elimination gives rows (1,3,-5,6), (0,1,3,-4), and (0,0,0,-9), so there is no solution. For q-40028, the excluded input satisfies 9a-18=0, giving a=2. For q-20590, back substitution gives (x,y,z)=(0,-2,1); for q-131590 it gives (-6,1,1); for q-10644 it gives (7,-5,-10). Their coefficient matrices are invertible, so their RREFs are the identity augmented by those solutions. For q-10636, elimination yields z=0, y=0, x=0 and RREF [I|0]. Its last operation is incorrectly labeled R₂:=R₁-2R₂; the displayed transition requires R₁:=R₁-2R₂. This source typo does not change its correct final answer. Matrix choices containing M∼ express the same final matrices shown in the source.",
